7 Peculiar Issues Which According to Science Prolong Age
Science has explored everything possible between earth and heaven.
These things have been proven to bring extra years into a person's life.
Some of the things are habits that directly or indirectly affect a person's health so that their lives are lengthened.
On the other hand, sometimes things that the person themselves cannot influence can bring them additional years.
These include, for example, a tendency to abdominal obesity or social status.
Regular shopping can prolong your age.
You don't always have to splurge - it's enough just to pick up a can of milk.
Efforts have been made to find out the secret of longevity through various studies.
The Medical Daily presented the seven strangest research results.
According to science, all of these things may bring more years of life.
Beer and coffee
Coffee consumption has been found to protect against some cancers, type 2 diabetes, Alzheimer's and Parkinson's diseases.
A Harvard University study found that moderate coffee consumption is associated with a "reduced risk of death," especially in neurological or cardiac diseases.
Again, alcohol is supported by studies, according to which moderate consumption - from one to three daily doses - may prolong life.
For example, one noticed that wine drinkers lived older than people who didn't drink at all.
Regular floss use can prolong a person's life by more than six years, one study says.
The argument is based on the fact that this prevents ingestivities.
They, on the other hand, can contribute to the onset of other diseases elsewhere in the human body.
A study carried out in Norway investigated how laughing affected a person's lifespan.
The seven-year project monitored more than 54 000 people.
Those who laughed more were 35 percent more likely to survive after the experiment ended.
According to many studies, sex, when the protection against sexually transmitted diseases has been taken into account, is good for health.
In addition, it can also prolong life.
Unfortunately, just having sex as such isn't enough.
In order for a person to have extra years in their life, they also need to have an orgasm.
Of course, physical activity brings additional years, there is no denying it.
However, achieving a long age does not require unconditionality.
According to one study by the University of Oxford, women with big buttocks had lower cholesterol levels.
There were also more omega 3 fatty acids in their bodies.
The same study linked these issues to lower mortality.
Whether it's an athlete who won an Olympic medal, or an Oscar-winning actor, he's more likely to live further than an ordinary chubby.
Many studies have tried to find the cause of this phenomenon.
One explanation may be that an ambitious person is likely to live in a way that will bringing additional years into their life.
Some researchers, on the other hand, suspect that long life is due to a person's social status - which, for its part, makes it possible, for example, to seek recognition such as the Nobel Prize.
A study of the purchasing behavior of people over the age of 65 found that a person who shops on a daily basis was likely to be older than someone who shops less often.
This is due to the fact that running in concrete stores reduces loneliness.
Again, it has been found to trigger biological mechanisms that may bring forward death.
Therefore, count the credit card from your hand - online shopping therefore does not have the same effect.
