KSML: This part of the new readiness troops will first go into battle in a war situation
In an acute war situation, conscripts are only ordered to take combat missions several months after swearing a military oath, Keskisuomalainen says.
According to Brigadier General Jukka Sonninen, interviewed by the Finnish Defence Forces' training commander interviewed by the magazine, for example, conscripts serving for 5.5 months in a war situation are only those who are in the final stages of their training.
According to the head of education, reservists belonging to the contingency forces will first be assigned.
